Sub-decomposes W22.5's `mds_tilemap_bg` parent bucket into 3 named sub-
buckets + 1 derived residual, covering the dominant remaining single-
bucket engine-side slice (8.30 ms median = 28% of inter_flip on First
Cave Tier-2 heavy-music per iter K K3). Wave-28 refuted the iter K
residual-decomp prediction that the 12 ms unmeasured slice lived inside
`phase=total`; instead it lives in `engine_tick - phase=total` ~ 24 ms,
and `mds_tilemap_bg` is its largest unmeasured sub-slice. Cutting it in
half (~4 ms) lands the session 40 fps goal.

Brackets (at game.cpp:605-636 inside W22.5's MdsTilemapBgTimer scope):
  mdt_bg_backdrop   -- map_draw_backdrop() at game.cpp:609. BK_FASTLEFT_-
                      LAYERS parallax / BK_FOLLOW / BK_FIXED dispatch.
                      H-A hypothesis: 2-5 ms.
  mdt_bg_tilelayer  -- map_draw(false) at game.cpp:610. BG tile layer
                      render via _tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop --
                      slot 0117's drawTileFast call site lives here.
                      H-B hypothesis: 3-6 ms.
  mdt_bg_tintscreen -- tintScreen() at game.cpp:614 (only when
                      settings->lights=on; full 320x240 INDEX8
                      darkening pass). H-C hypothesis: 0.5-4 ms.
  mdt_bg_residual   -- derived. g_mds_tilemap_bg_dt_this_tick - sum(3
                      sub-buckets); clamped 0. Self-validation:
                      median <0.5 ms => brackets exhaustive.

Implementation pattern: RAII (matches W22.5 / W22A / W20B game.cpp
convention; NOT the inline pattern used by W28 in Renderer.cpp -- game.cpp
mode_draw_scene work uses RAII, Renderer.cpp flip()-side uses inline).
Three new RAII timer structs in diagnostic_timers.h:
MdtBgBackdropTimer / MdtBgTilelayerTimer / MdtBgTintscreenTimer.

Critical placement decision per contract sec. 4: MdtBgTintscreenTimer scope
lives INSIDE the `if (settings->lights)` conditional, NOT outside. When
lights=off the timer never constructs (no SDL_GetTicksNS cost) and the
bucket emits n=0 placeholder per sec. 3 -- uniform 4-line per-block log
shape regardless of scene's lighting state.

Residual block lives in `game_tick_normal()` immediately after the W22.5
residual block (parent total `g_mds_tilemap_bg_dt_this_tick` is written
by W22.5's MdsTilemapBgTimer destructor inside DrawScene() at line 636;
the value is readable in game_tick_normal post-DrawScene-return).

Gated on SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MDS_BG_INSTR=1 (NEW; strict-1 per CLAUDE.md
convention; family-prefix consistency with W25's MDS_TFG_INSTR). Default
OFF. Cached static-const-bool -- -O2 hoists per-tick guards. Pairs with
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1 (W22.5) for the residual: the
parent total is gated on MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR; without it the residual
silently clamps to 0 (sub-bucket samples remain valid). Operator's W29A
iter sets both hints + the lower 3 layers (W20A + W20B + W22A) per
contract sec. 6.

Per-tick overhead when env unset: ~3 SDL_GetTicksNS reads (RAII
construction always fires; 2 always + 1 conditional on lights) + 3
conditional branches (RAII destructors gate on cached static-const-bool)
= sub-us cumulative. Will not measurably regress fps; PLAY2 control
parity (W29A2) confirms empirically against iter L baseline.

Storage: 3 sample arrays + 3 idxes + 3 per-tick dt locals + 1 residual
array + 1 residual idx (~3 KB static state at file scope in Renderer.cpp's
NXE::Diag block). Reuses W22.5's g_eng_tick_block_size = 100 cadence
(per contract sec. 3 -- NO new block_size constant).

Emit site: _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit() in Renderer.cpp, AFTER the
W22.5 [mode-draw-scene-stat] block and BEFORE the W23 [mds-tilemap-cache]
block. Output ordering: flip-stat -> flip-body-stat -> engine-tick-stat ->
mode-tick-stat -> mode-draw-scene-stat -> mds-bg-stat (NEW; layer 5.5) ->
mds-tilemap-cache -> mds-tfg-stat -> mds-tfg-tiles -> counters. Distinct
prefix `mds-bg-stat` so 8-layer grep stays clean. Empty-block placeholder
(n=0; 0.00 numerics) emitted for sub-buckets with no firings + a full
4-line placeholder block when env is set but no residual samples landed
(e.g. `flipacceltime` skip path engaged every tick in the block).

`mds_bg_instr_active()` accessor at file-scope-after-both-namespace-
closes block per W20B build-fix amendment (avoids nested
NXE::Graphics::NXE::Diag trap).

Direct-VESA-aware gating per `direct_vesa_aware_instrumentation_gating.md`:
gate counter = `g_mdt_bg_residual_idx` (game_tick_normal-anchored; ticks
under DV default since game_tick_normal runs regardless of which SDL
flush path is engaged). Emit fields = per-tick dt locals (no internal
sticky-state).

Strict-"1" match: only literal `1` activates; any other value (unset,
empty, "0") is OFF.

Goal: disambiguate H-A/H-B/H-C for the 8 ms `mds_tilemap_bg` slice
(28% of inter_flip); the dominant sub-bucket determines wave-30 lever
pick (BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS parallax cache vs map_draw(false) sub-decomp
vs tintScreen LUT swap).

Workspace-local; never upstreamed.

See docs/PHASE11-WAVE-29-CONTRACT.md for the full bracket-scheme
rationale + sec. 10 wave-30 decision tree.
